<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Security Features Demo</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: sans-serif; margin: 40px; }
    h1 { color: #333; }
    h2 { color: #666; margin-top: 30px; }
    .demo { background: #f5f5f5; padding: 15px; border-radius: 5px; margin: 10px 0; }
    .demo strong { color: #0066cc; }
    pre { background: #eee; padding: 10px; border-radius: 3px; overflow-x: auto; }
    .safe { color: green; }
    .unsafe { color: red; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Security Features Demo</h1>

  <h2>1. Sanitize Filter (DOMPurify)</h2>
  <p>The sanitize filter removes dangerous HTML tags using DOMPurify.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <h3>Raw User Input (XSS Risk)</h3>
    <p><strong>Input:</strong> <code>{{ userInput }}</code></p>
    <p class="unsafe">⚠️ Never render raw user input without sanitization!</p>
  </div>

  <div class="demo">
    <h3>Sanitized Output</h3>
    <p><strong>Input:</strong> <code>{{ userInput |> sanitize }}</code></p>
    <p class="safe">✓ Script tags removed by DOMPurify!</p>
  </div>

  <div class="demo">
    <h3>More Examples</h3>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Raw</th><th>Sanitized</th></tr>
      <tr><td><code>{{ dangerousHtml }}</code></td><td><code>{{ dangerousHtml |> sanitize }}</code></td></tr>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>2. Auto-toJSON in Script Context</h2>
  <p>When outputting values inside &lt;script&gt; tags with autoescape enabled, objects are automatically JSON-encoded.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <h3>Object in Script Tag</h3>
    <pre><code>&lt;script&gt;
  const config = {{ configData |> tojson }};
  const user = {{ userData |> tojson }};
&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
    <p class="safe">✓ Objects are automatically JSON-encoded (no need for manual tojson filter)</p>
  </div>

  <h2>3. Context-Aware Escaping</h2>
  <p>The escaping is context-aware. Different contexts require different escaping:</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <h3>HTML Context</h3>
    <p><code>{{ htmlContent }}</code> - Escaped for HTML</p>
  </div>

  <div class="demo">
    <h3>Attribute Context</h3>
    <p><code>&lt;div data-value="{{ attrContent }}"&gt;{{ htmlContent }}&lt;/div&gt;</code></p>
  </div>

  <h2>4. dompurify Config Option</h2>
  <p>You can customize DOMPurify behavior via the dompurify config option:</p>
  <pre><code>const engineConfig = {
  autoescape: true,
  dompurify: {
    ALLOWED_TAGS: ['b', 'i', 'em', 'strong'],
    ALLOWED_ATTR: ['href']
  }
};</code></pre>
</body>
</html>
